    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Tết: the most important festival",
     "texto": [
      "**Tết** (or **Tết Nguyên Đán**) is the New Year according to the **âm lịch** (lunar calendar). It usually falls between late January and February (**dương lịch** = solar calendar). The whole country has almost a week off.",
      "Everyone tries to **về quê ăn Tết** = go back to their home village to celebrate Tết with their family. If you go with your wife, it's your big family exam!",
      "You eat **bánh chưng** (square rice cake of glutinous rice with meat and beans), buy flowers (**hoa đào** in the north, **hoa mai** in the south) and make offerings to the ancestors (**cúng tổ tiên**).",
      "**xông nhà**: the first person to enter a house on day 1 brings luck (or bad luck) for the whole year. Children are given **lì xì** (money in a red envelope).",
      "• The key phrase: **Chúc mừng năm mới!** = Happy New Year!"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
